    <string name="intro_1_title">Read first, without read receipts</string>
    <string name="intro_1_body">KakaoTalk and text notifications are kept on this phone only. The sender still sees the message as unread.</string>
    <string name="intro_2_title">Swipe the screen edge to open</string>
    <string name="intro_2_body">From any app, swipe the handle inward to open the recent messages panel.</string>
    <string name="intro_2_swipe">← Swipe</string>
    <string name="intro_3_title">Reply in KakaoTalk</string>
    <string name="intro_3_body">Messages are marked as read only when you tap “Open in KakaoTalk”. Until then, you are just peeking.</string>
    <string name="intro_3_tag">Only when you reply</string>
    <string name="intro_sample_1">Where should we meet tonight?</string>
    <string name="intro_sample_2">Is 7 okay?</string>
    <string name="help_title">Help</string>
    <string name="help_replay_intro">Replay intro ›</string>
    <string name="help_q_not_saved">Messages are not being saved</string>
    <string name="help_a_not_saved">1. In KakaoTalk settings → Notifications, turn on message preview\n2. While KakaoTalk for PC is in use, your phone gets no notifications, so nothing is saved\n3. Chats with notifications turned off are not saved\n4. Turn off battery optimization for SecretNoti</string>
    <string name="help_check_permissions">Check permissions ›</string>
    <string name="help_q_read">When are messages marked as read?</string>
    <string name="help_a_read">Viewing in SecretNoti never marks messages as read. They are marked as read when you open the chat in KakaoTalk or tap “Open in KakaoTalk”.</string>
    <string name="help_q_stuck">A chat stays in the panel</string>
    <string name="help_a_stuck">If you clear all notifications and then open KakaoTalk directly, SecretNoti cannot tell. It catches up when the next message arrives, or you can swipe the chat out of the panel.</string>
    <string name="help_q_handle">The handle is missing or will not swipe</string>
    <string name="help_a_handle">In Settings → Edge panel, turn on Show handle and check the display-over-other-apps permission. If swiping triggers Back, turn on the gesture option or move the handle.</string>
    <string name="help_q_menu">Where is the chat menu?</string>
    <string name="help_a_menu">Long-press a chat to pin, hide, stop saving, or delete its history. Drag the panel edge to change its width.</string>
    <string name="help_q_apps">Which apps are supported?</string>
    <string name="help_a_apps">KakaoTalk, Messages, Teams, Telegram, and most apps that send message notifications. Turn them on or off in Settings → Saving.</string>
    <string name="help_request_app">Request an app ›</string>
    <string name="help_q_storage">Where are my messages stored?</string>
    <string name="help_a_storage">Only on this phone. SecretNoti has no internet permission, so it cannot send anything out. Use a backup file when you change phones.</string>
    <string name="help_q_deleted">How are deleted messages shown?</string>
    <string name="help_a_deleted">If the sender deletes a message, SecretNoti keeps the original and marks it with a dashed border and “Deleted”. You can also get an alert in Settings → Privacy.</string>
    <string name="help_contact">Still stuck? Contact us</string>
